sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2, superseding the Pass 1 audit (overall 82.7). The linear critical wavelength remains 1.939 mm with Pearson r = 0.9999998 and RMSE = 2.13e-4. The unbiased saturated wavelength is 2.216 mm on both the 8-wavelength patch (Pass 1) and the 16-wavelength patch (Pass 2), so the shift is not a coarse-bin artifact: the 16-wavelength box could have peaked at 2.068 mm or 1.939 mm and peaked at 2.216 mm. A midrib template of amplitude 0.004 at 1.939 mm entrains the field to 1.939 mm and raises the horizontal-edge fraction from 0.286 to 0.934, against 0.433 on the crown photograph. The photograph has no scale bar. Equal-diffusion ablation is unchanged (sigma_max -0.0615, std ratio 0.018). Weighted score 85.1/100. R4 and R5 remain open. Overall 85.1/100 (faithfulness 83.9, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 482774 B, 1260×840 px, artifact_sha256 03cd6470ad1f2e0c96035a526cc11c007ca6c7d277e0ce3b10f118dbd7798fe8 (sha256 03cd6470ad1f2e0c96035a526cc11c007ca6c7d277e0ce3b10f118dbd7798fe8), spec_fingerprint 889436d47b7f6a20b524144198f645dcccbc348d99fd9ce666f715dfafc2a48a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 889436d47b7f6a20b524144198f645dcccbc348d99fd9ce666f715dfafc2a48a; artifact_sha256: 03cd6470ad1f2e0c96035a526cc11c007ca6c7d277e0ce3b10f118dbd7798fe8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0/cornus_controversa_specimen.jpg=be3da2bb8b817bec..., datasets/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=61581ec4249a6ec3...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and the diffusion-driven instability conditions | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Xiang et al. 2006 place Cornus controversa in extant Cornus; this chronoseries is the Holocene tip only | Public-domain Meise Botanic Garden photograph of C. controversa 'Variegata'; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-specific rates a=0.06, b=0.94 and diffusivities that pin the linear lambda_c to 1.939 mm | Unbiased nonlinear wavelength 2.216 mm on a 16-wavelength patch, plus a separate entraining template | Explicit statement that the crown frame has no scale bar; transfer_boundary: 1.939 mm is the catalog detail scale for the linear law, not a length measured on the photograph | The template shows that a weak midrib cue can override the nonlinear peak; it is not evidence that the leaf has that cue; does_not_claim: That the Variegata cream margin is a Turing pattern | That pagoda tiers are chemical stripes | That the saturated pattern selects 1.939 mm in the absence of a template | A fossil predecessor inside this 1/1 chronoseries." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved. The 2.216 mm peak survives on a 16-wavelength patch, which has a bin at 2.068 mm between 2.216 and 1.939. It is a nonlinear shift, not a coarse-bin accident.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved. Bias 0.004 is executed as a separate template. It entrains lambda to 1.939 mm and is not substituted for the unbiased field.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Resolved. resolution_limit records scale_bar_present false and mm_per_px null.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': \"Open. No second assessor. This score is still the builder's own.\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Open. ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent, so the nanopubs are not signed.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.851"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent round; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

